# The upstream files this platform is a function of, at edk2-stable202602.
#
# `image/ovmf/default.nix` runs `sha256sum -c` on this from the edk2 source root
# and refuses to build on a mismatch. The point is the direction a bump breaks
# things in: our derived copies are static text, so if edk2 moves underneath them
# the build would otherwise succeed and quietly keep serving the old logic --
# including through a security fix. A hash makes that loud.
#
# Two kinds of file are listed, for two different reasons:
#
#   DERIVED FROM -- Library/NoShimQemuLoadImageLib and Driver/QemuLoaderFs are
#   copies of the first four with small, documented edits. If the original
#   changes, the edit has to be re-applied to the new text, not left behind.
#
#   INHERITED    -- EnclavidFw.dsc `!include`s AmdSevX64.dsc, and EnclavidFw.fdf
#   is a copy of AmdSevX64.fdf. Changes to the DSC arrive automatically, which
#   is exactly why they should be read: the commit that introduced the shim path
#   this platform removes did not touch either of these files, so a diff that
#   looks empty here is not permission to skip reviewing the modules.
#
# WHEN THIS FAILS: read the upstream diff, re-run the generators, review THEIR
# diff, then update the hash here. The failure is the review request; updating
# the number without reading is how the review stops happening.
#
# The four modules whose behaviour this image depends on, in the order they
# matter, are named in `image/ovmf/default.nix`.

